{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Legislate to abolish royal prerogative powers & give them to Parliament",
        "additional_details": "The Crown\u2019s prerogative are powers held or exercised in the Monarch\u2019s name. They include dissolving/opening Parliament, proroguing it, Royal Assent to Bills, appointing Prime Ministers/ministers, agreeing treaties, and being Head of the Armed Forces. King\u2019s Consent give the Crown advance sight of, and special consent procedure for bills affecting the Crown\u2019s powers. We believe all these powers should be handed to Parliament by statute.",
        "background": "Parliament should legislate to abolish the Crown\u2019s royal prerogative powers, including dissolution, prorogation, Royal Assent, appointments, treaties, Head of the Armed Forces, and King\u2019s Consent over certain legislation. We want to place these powers under Parliament\u2019s authority.",
